---
title: Oven Roasted Greek Lemon Potatoes
description: Oven Roasted Greek Lemon Potatoes Recipe is a flavorful side dish, bursting with zesty lemon, herbs, and perfectly crisp golden edges.
image: https://blessmyfoodbypayal.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/IMG_8110.png
source: https://blessmyfoodbypayal.com/oven-roasted-greek-lemon-potatoes-recipe
servings: '4'
cuisine: Greek
tags: potatoes, side, greek, vegan, gluten-free, roasted
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 50 minutes
course: Side Dish, snacks
---

Cut @potato{4}(big, around 680 grams) into wedges and put in @water till used. It will prevent them from turning brown.

Take a #baking dish{} and add @vegetable stock{about 1/2 cup}, @olive oil{1/4%cup}, @fresh lemon juice{1/4%cup}, @garlic{3-4%cloves}(chopped), @oregano{1%tsp}, @salt{to taste}, @black pepper powder{1/2%tsp}, and @lemon zest{1%tsp}. Mix them well.

Arrange potato wedges in the dish without overlapping each other.

Top with @lemon slices{3-4}(thin) here and there, though not necessary.

Bake in preheated oven 200°C for ~{40-45%minutes}.

Take the dish out and turn the sides of potatoes.

Bake further for ~{40-45%minutes} or until potatoes turn brown and tender. This is the stage when the entire liquid content in the dish is absorbed by potatoes, except oil.

If you want the wedges to be more crispy, bake more for ~{15-20%minutes}.

Greek Lemon Potatoes are ready. Arrange the potato wedges in a serving plate. Also drizzle the oil lying in the dish.

Garnish with @cilantro or @parsley{}(for garnish). Enjoy.